cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "abaqus-mcp: an MCP server for autonomous Abaqus/Standard FEA"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gulakala
    given-names: Rutwik
repository-code: "https://github.com/rutwikg/abaqus-mcp"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that drives Abaqus/Standard finite
  element analysis from natural language. It builds meshed models from a JSON
  simulation spec (parametric shapes or imported STEP/IGES CAD), submits jobs
  headless, and autonomously diagnoses and repairs solver failures by parsing
  the .sta / .msg / .dat outputs and patching the keyword deck before retrying.
keywords:
  - finite element analysis
  - Abaqus
  - Model Context Protocol
  - simulation automation
  - large language models
